In British English usage, policemen used to carry "truncheons", and now
carry "side-handled batons".  Prior to the adoption of the side-handled
baton (sometime in the past 10-15 years, can't remember exactly when) by
British police forces, the word "baton" was not used in British English
to denote the blunt weapon carried by a policeman.
